orth America】\nL59: \nL60: 【27†Sub-Saharan Africa】\nL61: \nL62: 【28†Multiple Regions / Worldwide】\nL63: ##### Formats\nL64: \nL65: 【29†Feature】\nL66: \nL67: 【30†Fact Sheet】\nL68: \nL69: 【31†Video】\nL70: \nL71: 【32†Data Essay】\nL72: \nL73:   * 【33†Publications】\nL74:   * 【34†Our Methods】\nL75:   * 【35†Short Reads】\nL76:   * 【36†Tools & Datasets】\nL77:   * 【37†Experts】\nL78:   * 【38†About Us】\nL79: \nL80:   *     * 【39†Research Topics】\nL81:     * 【33†Publications】\nL82:     * 【35†Short Reads】\nL83:     * 【40†Tools & Datasets】\nL84:     * 【38†About Pew Research Center】\nL85:     * 【41†Newsletters】\nL86:     * 【42†Press】\nL87:     * 【43†My Account】\nL88:     * 【5†Contacted By Us?】\nL89: \nL90:   * [Input: ]\nL91: \nL92: Read Our Research On:\nL93:     * 【6†Artificial Intelligence】\nL94:     * 【7†Donald Trump】\nL95:     * 【8†Middle East】\nL96: \nL97:   1. 【44†Attitudes on Same-Sex Marriage】\nL98: \nL99:   * Fact Sheet\nL100: \nL101: |\nL102: \nL103: May 14, 2019\nL104: # Attitudes on Same-Sex Marriage\nL105: \nL106: Table of Contents\nL107: \nL108:   1. 【44†Attitudes on Same-Sex Marriage】\nL109: ## Public opinion on same-sex marriage\nL110: \nL111: In Pew Research Center polling in 2004, Americans opposed same-sex marriage by a margin of 60% to 31%.\nL112: \nL113: Support for same-sex marriage has steadily grown over the past 15 years. And today, support for same-sex marriage remains near its highest point since Pew Research Center began polling on this issue. Based on polling in 2019, a majority of Americans (61%) support same-sex marriage, while 31% oppose it.\nL114: \nL115: * * *\nL116: \nL117: Same-sex marriage overall\nL118: % of U.S. adults who favor/oppose same-sex marriage (2001-2019)\nL119: \nL120: PEW RESEARCH CENTER\nL121: \nL122: * * *\nL123: \nL124: * * *\nL125: \nL126: Same-sex marriage overall\nL127: \nL128: % of U.S. adults who favor/oppose same-sex marriage (2001-2019)\nL129: Year  | Favor  | Oppose\nL130: --- | --- | ---\nL131: 2001  | 35%  | 57%\nL132: 2003  | 32%  | 59%\nL133: 2004  | 31%  | 60%\nL134: 2005  | 36%  | 53%\nL135: 2006  | 35%  | 55%\nL136: 2007  | 37%  | 54%\nL137: 2008  | 39%  | 51%\nL138: 2009  | 37%  | 54%\nL139: 2010  | 42%  | 48%\nL140: 2011  | 46%  | 44%\nL141: 2012  | 48%  | 43%\nL142: 2013  | 50%  | 43%\nL143: 2014  | 52%  | 40%\nL144: 2015  | 55%  | 39%\nL145: 2016  | 55%  | 37%\nL146: 2017  | 62%  | 32%\nL147: 2019  | 61%  | 31%\nL148: \nL149: * * *\nL150: \nL151: Download data as .csv\nL152: \nL153: PEW RESEARCH CENTER\nL154: \nL155: * * *\nL156: \nL157: [Button: Chart][Button: Data]\nL158: ## Attitudes on same-sex marriage by political party identification\nL159: \nL160: Three-quarters of Democrats and Democratic-leaning independents (75%) and fewer than half of Republicans and Republican leaners (44%) favor same-sex marriage.\nL161: \nL162: More independents who lean toward the Democratic Party (81%) favor gay marriage than Democrats (71%). Similarly, Republican leaners are more supportive (56%) than Republicans (37%).\nL163: Support for same-sex marriage now stands at 88% among self-described liberal Democrats and Democratic leaners and 64% among conservative and moderate Democrats. Fewer conservative Republicans and Republican leaners (36%) support same-sex marriage than moderate and liberal Republicans (59%).\nL164: ### Tab Contents\nL165: \nL166: * * *\nL167: \nL168: Leaned party\nL169: \nL170: % of U.S. adults who favor same-sex marriage, by political party identification (2001-2019)\nL171: \nL172: PEW RESEARCH CENTER\nL173: \nL174: * * *\nL175: \nL176: * * *\nL177: \nL178: Leaned party\nL179: \nL180: % of U.S. adults who favor same-sex marriage, by political party identification (2001-2019)\nL181: Year  | Rep/Lean Rep  | Dem/Lean Dem\nL182: --- | --- | ---\nL183: 2001  | 23%  | 45%\nL184: 2003  | 24%  | 44%\nL185: 2004  | 19%  | 43%\nL186: 2005  | 20%  | 49%\nL187: 2006  | 20%  | 47%\nL188: 2007  | 20%  | 49%\nL189: 2008  | 23%  | 51%\nL190: 2009  | 21%  | 51%\nL191: 2010  | 27%